{define: Cadd9 base-fret 1 frets x 3 2 0 3 0} 
{define: D4 base-fret 1 frets x x 0 2 3 3}
{define: F base-fret 1 frets x x 3 2 1 1} 
{define: Fmaj7 base-fret 1 frets x 3 3 2 1 0} 
{define: Gadd base-fret 1 frets 3 2 0 0 3 3} 
{t: FOR EMILY, WHEREVER I MAY FIND HER (In C) - Simon and Garfunkel}
{st: (Simon)}
{artist: Simon and Garfunkel}
{composer: Paul Simon}


https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=kOgmYFTZ2iU  (Capo 0)

This version is from their Greatest Hits album and they do it in C.  On the album "Parsley, Sage, Rosemary and Thyme," and also how S & G usually did it live, it's in the key of D. 

TIP:  If transposing, play the root chord of the transposed (Gadd) adding the 5th note as necessary.

TIP:  Fingerpick the opening if you can, otherwise the sequence is four strums of the (G)/(Gadd) covering the 2nd string/3rd fret on the 3rd strum.  (Cadd9) is just (C) with pinky added to the 2nd string/3rd fret.  Each sequence is played 4 time.  During the final (C)(Cadd9) set slow down for the final strum to set up the opening of the song.  Note to self:  begin with the 2nd string on both (Gadd) and (Cadd9).

TIP:  (D4) is just (D) with pinky added to the 1st string/3rd fret.  (Fmaj7) is just (F) with the bottom string open.


